    "body": "_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: follows #432 (merged into main); independent of the open DEVONthink stack (#415, #418-#421) and #426.\n- Depends on: #432 (merged). It replaces `sp-citations--half-frame-columns` and the load-time widths from that PR.\n- If merged out of order with the others: no conflict expected; they touch other parts of `sp-academic.org`.\n- After merging: nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Real frame size:** the columns come from the frame Emacs has on the screen (`sp-citations--frame-columns`): the text width of the selected frame in pixels divided by the pixel width of a character of the `default` face (so a font change shows at once, before the frame is resized). While the posframe is on in a graphical frame it takes `sp-posframe-width-fraction` of that, as `sp-posframe-get-size` does. The assumed half-display and AeroSpace gaps are gone.\n- **Dynamic:** `sp-citations--apply-layout` runs before `citar-select-ref` and `citar-select-refs` (so before `citar-open`, `citar-insert-citation` and `citar-create-note`). It compares the state (columns, character width, font family and height) with the last one and only then makes the emoji cells and the templates again. A command in an unchanged frame and font costs nothing.\n- **Fix for \"`sp-citations-fit-layout` does nothing on a font change\":** two causes found in citar's source.\n  - `citar-refresh` does not exist in current citar, so my guarded call (`(when (fboundp 'citar-refresh) ...)`) never ran, in this module and in the earlier docs.\n  - citar keeps every candidate as a pre-formatted string, made when the bibliography is read or when the format string changes. The type emoji cells are in those strings, so with the same templates after a font change nothing made citar format them again. Now, when only the font changed, `sp-citations--repreformat` calls `citar-cache--preformat-bibliography` on the cached bibliographies (no file is read); when the templates change citar does it by itself.\n- **Kept:** column order emoji, author, year, title, citekey, keywords; pixel-exact emoji cells; `sp-citations-layout-columns` to override; `M-x sp-citations-fit-layout` to force it.\n- **Not done:** no `window-size-change-functions` hook; a resize while the prompt is open applies at the next command.\n- **Other places that call `citar-refresh`:** `sp-bibprocess.el` (the long-key fix and `sp-academic.org` lines 2778/2874) also guard it with `fboundp`, so they are harmless no-ops; I did not change them here.\n- Tests: `tests/sp-citations-layout-test.el`, 7 pass (columns follow pixel width, character width and posframe mode; the state change makes the templates and, for a font-only change, the re-preformat; plus the layout and emoji-cell tests). Tangle check passes.\n- Docs updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists). No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude: GUI)\n- [ ] Half-frame tile: `C-c w b o`; note the column widths and that nothing wraps (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-g`, maximize the frame, `C-c w b o` again: the columns are wider (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-g`, back to the half tile, open again: narrow again\n- [ ] Font size: `M-+` or `M--` a few steps, `C-g`, `C-c w b o`: the emoji cells and columns follow the new size with no manual command (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-citations-fit-layout`: it prints the column count; the next open is aligned\n- [ ] `M-: (sp-citations--frame-columns)` in each size and font: tell me the numbers\n- [ ] Citekey shows 45 characters once the frame gives 110 columns or more\n- [ ] Regression: `citar-insert-citation` and `citar-create-note` work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/citar-layout-follows-frame` (the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed).\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- No notes or vault files change, so nothing to restore there.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW",
